  (clause (text "a signaling-NaN input to a conversion raises NV;") (properties "snan-conversion-invalid") (properties "snan-conversion-canonical"))
  (clause (text "the integer conversions saturate with NV as FCVT.int.S does;") (properties "fcvt-wu-saturates") (properties "fcvt-invalid-flag") (properties "fcvt-w-nan") (properties "fcvt-wu-nan") (properties "fcvt-l-nan") (properties "fcvt-w-too-large") (properties "fcvt-w-negative-infinity") (properties "fcvt-l-too-large") (properties "fcvt-lu-negative"))
  (clause (text "and every D instruction is an illegal-instruction exception at mstatus.FS Off, with FS Dirty on any f-register write or flag change.") (properties "fs-off-cause") (properties "fs-off-keeps-rd") (properties "fs-off-load") (properties "fs-off-arithmetic") (properties "fs-dirty") (properties "fs-clean-stays") (properties "fs-flags-dirty") (properties "fs-dirty-sd") (limits "FS Off is witnessed on a move, a load and an arithmetic form, not on every form")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-SVADE")
  (clause (text "The profile implements Svade: when a translation needs an A or D PTE update, the hart raises a page fault instead of performing the hardware update.") (properties "both-set-loads") (properties "both-set-stores") (properties "a-clear-load-cause") (properties "a-clear-load-tval") (properties "a-clear-store-cause") (properties "a-clear-store-tval") (properties "d-clear-load-completes") (properties "d-clear-store-cause") (properties "d-clear-store-tval") (properties "a-clear-fetch-cause") (properties "a-clear-fetch-tval") (properties "pte-a-still-clear") (properties "pte-d-still-clear") (properties "pte-fetch-still-clear"))
  (clause (text "Three evidence legs: (i) the pinned revision defines exactly two A/D schemes and names the page-fault one Svade (RVP-SUPERVISOR §11.1.3.1, §11.1.10); (ii) the profile's own translation precedent — the U54 MMU the Sv39 choice already cites — implements exactly that scheme ('does not automatically set the A and D bits … Instead, the U54 MMU will raise a page fault', FU540 §4.7); (iii) the laboratory's observe-through-the-ISA discipline (P4-SYSTEM.2 decision 6) can evidence a page fault (scause/stval via csrr) but cannot evidence an implicit PTE write, so the hardware-update default would price a new observation vocabulary to test a side effect the laboratory need not produce.") (limits "why the profile chose Svade, its three evidence legs, is the selection's reasoning and not behaviour a run can witness"))
  (clause (text "Svadu is NOT selected: menvcfg's ADUE stays WPRI (the state document's wpri_62_0 field).") (properties "adue-stays-clear")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-SV39")
  (clause (text "Translation is Sv39:") (properties "sv39-taken") (properties "walk-4k") (properties "walk-2m") (properties "walk-1g") (properties "not-canonical-cause") (properties "not-canonical-tval") (properties "misaligned-superpage-cause"))
  (clause (text "of the three paged virtual-memory schemes defined for SXLEN=64 (Sv39, Sv48, Sv57), the profile selects the minimal Linux-capable one") (properties "bare-at-reset") (properties "sv48-from-bare") (properties "sv57-from-bare") (properties "sv48-over-sv39"))
  (clause (text "— also the one the pinned SoC precedent implements (the FU540-C000's U54 supports Bare and Sv39).") (limits "that the SoC precedent implements it is the selection's reasoning: no FU540 is run"))
  (clause (text "The U54's A/D behaviour (page faults instead of setting PTE A/D bits) is recorded as P4-SYSTEM.3's policy input, not as this profile's rule.") (limits "the U54's A and D behaviour is REQ-D-SVADE's, and this case takes no position on it")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-PRIV-MODES")
  (clause (text "The profile implements machine, supervisor and user modes") (properties "misa-names-the-modes") (properties "misa-s") (properties "misa-u") (properties "ecall-from-m") (properties "mpp-holds-u") (properties "mpp-holds-s") (properties "s-reads-sscratch") (properties "s-cannot-read-m") (properties "trap-recorded-s") (properties "ecall-from-s") (properties "u-cannot-read-s") (properties "trap-recorded-u") (properties "ecall-from-u"))
  (clause (text "— the minimum a Linux-capable profile needs (M-mode firmware, S-mode kernel, U-mode userspace);") (limits "that three modes are what Linux needs is the selection's reasoning: no Linux is run"))
  (clause (text "the hypervisor extension is excluded,") (properties "misa-no-h") (properties "no-h-state"))
  (clause (text "and every mode-dependent behaviour is tested in each supported mode (P4-SYSTEM.2).") (limits "that every mode-dependent behaviour is tested in each mode is a claim over the corpus and P4-SYSTEM.2, not this case's")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-FAULT-PRIORITY")
  (clause (text "Synchronous exceptions follow the pinned priority table (decreasing priority): the instruction-address translation faults,") (properties "fetch-page-over-decode-cause") (properties "fetch-page-over-decode-tval") (properties "fetch-page-over-access-cause") (properties "fetch-page-over-access-tval"))
  (clause (text "then the instruction access fault,") (properties "fetch-access-over-decode-cause") (properties "fetch-access-over-decode-tval"))
  (clause (text "then illegal-instruction, environment call and environment break,") (properties "illegal-cause") (properties "ecall-cause") (properties "ebreak-cause") (properties "illegal-over-misaligned-cause") (properties "illegal-over-translation-cause") (properties "illegal-over-access-cause"))
  (clause (text "then - the table's one implementation-defined position - load/store/AMO address-misaligned, which this profile takes HIGH, judged before the explicit access's translation (the laboratory's choice at P4-SYSTEM.3 decision 7;") (properties "misaligned-over-page-load-cause") (properties "misaligned-over-page-load-tval") (properties "misaligned-over-page-store-cause") (properties "misaligned-over-page-store-tval") (properties "misaligned-over-access-load-cause") (properties "misaligned-over-access-load-tval") (properties "misaligned-over-access-store-cause") (properties "misaligned-over-access-store-tval"))
  (clause (text "misaligned atomics take their declared access-fault codes at the same point),") (properties "atomic-lr-same-point-cause") (properties "atomic-lr-same-point-tval") (properties "atomic-amo-same-point-cause") (properties "atomic-amo-same-point-tval"))
  (clause (text "then the explicit access's translation faults (the first encountered),") (properties "aligned-on-invalid-cause") (properties "aligned-on-invalid-tval") (properties "aligned-store-on-invalid-cause") (properties "aligned-store-on-invalid-tval") (properties "translation-over-access-load-cause") (properties "translation-over-access-load-tval") (properties "translation-over-access-store-cause") (properties "translation-over-access-store-tval") (limits "an aligned access touches one page here and a misaligned one never reaches translation, so no two translation faults compete"))
  (clause (text "then its physical access fault.") (properties "physical-last-load-cause") (properties "physical-last-load-tval") (properties "physical-last-store-cause") (properties "physical-last-store-tval"))
  (clause (text "Instruction-address-misaligned is unreachable here (IALIGN 16 with C)") (properties "odd-target-reached"))
  (clause (text "and no breakpoint exists (no Sdtrig).") (limits "that no breakpoint exists is Sdtrig's absence from the selection: the derivation's vocabulary has no trigger CSR to read"))
  (clause (text "Every adjacent pair the profile can produce is pinned by a guest on both engines: the fetch fault over decode (fault-fetch), illegal-instruction over misaligned and over translation faults (prio-sv39's FS=Off cells, f-fs-off, d-fs-off), misaligned over page and access faults (it-prio-load, prio-sv39, a-amo-sv39), translation over the physical access (prio-sv39).") (limits "this one program holds each pair the statement names, and the guests it names stay in the corpus, each judged by its own expectations")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-ATOMIC-MISALIGN")
  (clause (text "Misaligned atomic accesses take the access-fault family by kind — 5 for LR (a load exception: RVP-MACHINE's exception table maps load-reserved to load exceptions),") (properties "lr-w-cause") (properties "lr-w-tval") (properties "lr-d-cause") (properties "lr-d-tval") (properties "lr-d-word-aligned-cause") (properties "lr-d-word-aligned-tval"))
  (clause (text "7 for SC/AMO (store/AMO exceptions):") (properties "sc-w-cause") (properties "sc-w-tval") (properties "sc-d-cause") (properties "sc-d-tval") (properties "amoadd-w-cause") (properties "amoadd-w-tval") (properties "amoswap-d-cause") (properties "amoswap-d-tval") (properties "rd-kept") (properties "memory-kept"))
  (clause (text "the specification offers misaligned-or-access-fault (RVI-A §12.1.2, §12.1.4) and the choice is reference-matched to the tracked Sail override's declared PMAs ((amo AccessFault) (lrsc AccessFault));") (limits "a misaligned AMO is judged before translation only with this case's own overlay: under the profile override the pinned binary judges it after"))
  (clause (text "judged before translation (the P4-SYSTEM.3 decision-7 hand-off).") (properties "translation-lr-cause") (properties "translation-lr-tval") (properties "translation-sc-cause") (properties "translation-sc-tval") (properties "translation-amo-cause") (properties "translation-amo-tval") (properties "aligned-lr-cause") (properties "aligned-lr-tval") (properties "aligned-amo-cause") (properties "aligned-amo-tval")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-RESERVATION")
  (clause (text "The one-hart laboratory selects a reservation (physical address, byte width, valid) covering exactly the most recent completed LR's word or doubleword.") (properties "exact-address") (properties "same-address-pairs") (properties "doubleword-pairs"))
  (clause (text "Exact physical/width matching and trap retention are selected profile policies within A12.1.2's latitude, not the architecture's unique invalidation policy.") (properties "misaligned-keeps-reservation") (limits "exact width is past the reference: the pinned binary pairs an SC of another width at the same address, so it is a selection this case states and does not compare"))
  (clause (text "A completed LR replaces the prior reservation.") (properties "lr-replaces-old") (properties "lr-replaces-new"))
  (clause (text "A completed SC invalidates it on success or failure at any address, clearing validity while retaining address/width bookkeeping.") (properties "failed-sc-at-b") (properties "failure-invalidates") (properties "first-sc-pairs") (properties "success-invalidates") (limits "the address and width a cleared reservation keeps have no effect while validity is clear, so nothing here observes them"))
  (clause (text "Alignment, Store translation and physical write permission must pass before SC can complete;") (properties "misaligned-sc-traps") (properties "no-write-permission-traps") (properties "translation-fault"))
  (clause (text "target faults preserve the prior validity, address, width and destination.") (properties "misaligned-keeps-rd") (properties "permission-keeps-reservation") (properties "translation-keeps-reservation"))
  (clause (text "Virtual aliases pair under this choice when physical address and width match.") (properties "alias-pairs"))
  (clause (text "Ordinary same-hart instructions preserve the reservation; direct witnesses include SW, SD, FSD, AMOADD, ADDI and FENCE.") (properties "sw-preserves") (properties "sd-preserves") (properties "fsd-preserves") (properties "amoadd-preserves") (properties "addi-preserves") (properties "fence-preserves"))
  (clause (text "The environment supplies no other-hart or device invalidations.") (limits "no other hart or device exists here to invalidate anything"))
  (clause (text "Cold reset starts at (0, 0, false) under the reset contract.") (properties "cold-no-reservation") (limits "only the cleared validity of the reset state is observable"))
  (clause (text "This selects one laboratory realization, not multicore behavior or all architecturally permitted reservation outcomes.") (limits "this selects one laboratory realization and claims nothing of multicore behaviour")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-SC-DETERMINISTIC")
  (clause (text "The selected single-hart laboratory makes completed SC deterministic after natural alignment, Store translation and physical write permission pass.") (properties "sc-w-result") (properties "sc-d-result"))
  (clause (text "A valid reservation at the same physical address and exact byte width succeeds without spurious failure: store rs2's low-width bytes and write result 0 to rd.") (properties "sc-w-low-bytes") (properties "sc-d-all-bytes"))
  (clause (text "Otherwise completed SC writes failure code 1 and issues no data Load or Store;") (properties "beside-fails") (properties "failure-stores-nothing") (properties "no-second-store"))
  (clause (text "it still obtains side-effect-free physical StorePermission.") (properties "permission-before-failure") (properties "translation-before-failure"))
  (clause (text "Source and address use the original register values, including destination aliases;") (properties "rd-is-rs2-result") (properties "rd-is-rs2-stored") (properties "rd-is-rs1-result") (properties "rd-is-rs1-stored"))
  (clause (text "rd=x0 discards only the result.") (properties "rd-x0-stored"))
  (clause (text "Any completed SC clears reservation validity while retaining address/width bookkeeping.") (properties "completed-clears") (properties "rd-x0-completed") (limits "the address and width a cleared reservation keeps have no effect while validity is clear, so nothing here observes them"))
  (clause (text "Target faults do not complete SC: they preserve the prior reservation and destination and report the virtual fault address.") (properties "fault-keeps-destination") (properties "target-fault-cause") (properties "target-fault-vaddr") (properties "target-fault-keeps-reservation"))
  (clause (text "Translation reads and TLB fills may precede completion or a target fault;") (limits "translation reads and TLB fills have no observation in this vocabulary"))
  (clause (text "Svade performs no implicit PTE update.") (properties "svade-no-update"))
  (clause (text "The most recent completed LR and intervening completed SC determine reservation history under REQ-D-RESERVATION.") (limits "reservation history as a whole is REQ-D-RESERVATION's case"))
  (clause (text "Exact-width matching, physical-alias pairing, failure code 1 and no spurious failure are selected laboratory policies within A12.1.2/12.1.3's latitude, not every permitted architecture outcome or a multicore progress claim.") (limits "exact width is past the reference, physical-alias pairing is REQ-D-RESERVATION's case, and this claims nothing of multicore progress")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-GC-COMPOSITION")
  (clause (text "The profile's instruction set is RV64I plus the extensions M, A, F, D and C,") (properties "misa-letters") (properties "rv64i-width") (properties "m-present") (properties "a-present") (properties "a-stored") (properties "f-present") (properties "d-present") (properties "c-present"))
  (clause (text "plus Zicsr and Zifencei, plus Zicntr:") (properties "zicsr-present") (properties "zifencei-present") (properties "zicntr-present"))
  (clause (text "'G' is the defined abbreviation for the IMAFDZicsr_Zifencei base-and-extensions combination,") (limits "that G abbreviates this combination is the naming chapter's definition, not behaviour a run can witness"))
  (clause (text "and this profile is G plus C and Zicntr on the unprivileged side and Sstc on the privileged side.") (properties "sstc-present")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-EXT-CLOSURE")
  (clause (text "The extension dependency closure is complete under the pinned revision: D depends on F;") (properties "d-narrows-to-f") (properties "f-boxed-in-d") (properties "f-reads-unboxed-as-nan"))
  (clause (text "F depends on Zicsr for control and status register access;") (properties "fcsr-holds-flags") (properties "fflags-through-zicsr") (properties "frm-through-zicsr") (properties "fcsr-composes"))
  (clause (text "and C decomposes as Zca always plus Zcd when D is present (Zcf exists only at RV32).") (properties "zca-present") (properties "zcd-stores") (properties "zcd-loads") (properties "zcf-absent-rd") (properties "zcf-absent-fd"))
  (clause (text "Nothing in this profile is inferred from the letter 'G' alone.") (limits "that nothing is inferred from the letter G is how the catalogue is written, not behaviour a run can witness")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-PRIV-REVISION")
  (clause (text "The privileged architecture is the pinned publication's: Machine-Level ISA Version 1.13") (properties "mstatus-xlen-fields") (properties "menvcfg-exists") (properties "menvcfg-holds-stce") (limits "the pinned binary tells no guest 1.12 from 1.13: none of the 198 guests' verdicts moved under 1.12, so this witnesses what arrived after 1.11, and 1.13 itself is the pinned sources' identity"))
  (clause (text "and Supervisor-Level ISA Version 1.13,") (properties "sstatus-view") (properties "stimecmp-in-s"))
  (clause (text "under spec revision v20260120 — the same publication family as the unprivileged pin.") (limits "the publication family is the pinned sources' identity, not behaviour a run can witness")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-RVWMO")
  (clause (text "The memory consistency model is RVWMO:") (properties "own-store") (properties "fence-all") (properties "fence-rw") (properties "fence-tso") (limits "a single hart cannot tell RVWMO from a stronger model: nothing here reorders, so this is what one hart sees of it"))
  (clause (text "with the A extension in the profile the memory model is load-bearing even at one hart (the AMOs and their aq/rl annotations),") (properties "amo-plain") (properties "amo-aq") (properties "amo-rl") (properties "amo-aqrl") (properties "amo-all-stored") (properties "lr-aq") (properties "sc-rl"))
  (clause (text "and the multicore exposure of the weak model is MC-MULTICORE's, never smuggled in.") (limits "the multicore exposure is MC-MULTICORE's, and this claims nothing of it")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-PRIV-INSNS")
  (clause (text "The privileged instructions in scope are mret, sret, wfi and sfence.vma (the pinned privileged instruction listings);") (properties "wfi-retires") (properties "sfence-retires") (properties "mret-executes") (properties "sret-executes") (limits "the pinned author refuses every other SYSTEM word, so the listings' other instructions are not shown refused"))
  (clause (text "wfi's wake semantics belong to the interrupt/counter/wait leaf (P4-SYSTEM.5).") (limits "wfi's wake semantics are P4-SYSTEM.5's, and each wfi here has an interrupt pending")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-GC-PRIV-INSNS")
  (clause (text "The privileged system instructions behave per mode: mret/sret execute in their mode or higher and raise illegal-instruction below it") (properties "ecall-from-s") (properties "mret-in-s") (properties "mret-in-u") (properties "sret-in-u") (properties "sret-in-m") (properties "sret-reached-u"))
  (clause (text "(sret also raises in S when mstatus.TSR=1);") (properties "sret-tsr"))
  (clause (text "a legal wfi enters the wait - it retires, then the hart stalls and issues no fetch until a locally-enabled pending interrupt (at any privilege level, regardless of the global enables and of mideleg) wakes it, the no-op latitude recorded but not taken;") (properties "wfi-wakes-undelegated") (properties "wfi-wakes-delegated") (properties "wfi-in-s") (limits "the stall's length and the fetches it withholds are not observed: each wfi here wakes at once, and no-op latitude is the catalogue's selection"))
  (clause (text "wfi raises illegal-instruction in U (S is present) and in S when mstatus.TW=1;") (properties "wfi-tw") (properties "wfi-in-u") (limits "TW is tested on an idle hart: with an interrupt pending under TW the reference completes the wfi and the laboratory refuses it, as the specification lets each do"))
  (clause (text "sfence.vma raises illegal-instruction in U and in S with mstatus.TVM=1,") (properties "sfence-in-u") (properties "sfence-tvm"))
  (clause (text "and invalidates the modelled TLB by the specification's four rs1/rs2 cases.") (properties "before-the-fences") (properties "sfence-all") (properties "sfence-va") (properties "sfence-asid") (properties "sfence-va-asid"))
  (clause (text "xRET pops the two-level privilege stack (xIE<-xPIE, mode<-xPP, xPIE<-1, xPP<-U),") (properties "mret-pops") (properties "sret-pops"))
  (clause (text "clears MPRV when the target is not M,") (properties "mret-clears-mprv"))
  (clause (text "and sets pc<-xepc.") (properties "mret-sets-pc") (properties "sret-sets-pc")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-NO-H")
  (clause (text "The hypervisor extension is excluded:") (properties "misa-no-h") (properties "mstatus-no-h-bits") (properties "mideleg-no-vs") (properties "mie-no-vs") (limits "hstatus and the other H state are past the pinned author's vocabulary, so H's absence is read from misa, mstatus, mideleg and mie"))
  (clause (text "the profile has one hart and no virtualization workload in the first Linux profile;") (properties "one-hart") (limits "that no virtualization workload needs it is the selection's reasoning, not behaviour a run can witness"))
  (clause (text "H would arrive with a consumer, never ahead of one.") (limits "that H arrives with a consumer is a rule for later, not behaviour a run can witness")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-NO-PMP")
  (clause (text "PMP is excluded at v0:") (properties "s-load") (properties "s-store") (properties "u-load") (properties "u-store") (limits "S and U fetching with nothing configured is witnessed by every case that runs there and not by this one: a refused fetch reads as absent evidence, not as a difference, so the alternative could not compare it"))
  (clause (text "the privileged architecture's physical memory protection unit is optional,") (limits "pmpcfg0 and pmpaddr0 are past the pinned author's vocabulary, so the CSRs' absence is not read"))
  (clause (text "and the first boot contract does not require it;") (limits "that the first boot contract does not require it, and that a board branch may revisit it, are the selection's reasoning, not behaviour a run can witness"))
  (clause (text "the decision is revisited by the board branch that needs it.") (limits "that the first boot contract does not require it, and that a board branch may revisit it, are the selection's reasoning, not behaviour a run can witness")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-ENDIAN")
  (clause (text "Little-endian.") (properties "byte-0") (properties "byte-7") (properties "half-0") (properties "word-4") (properties "no-big-endian-bits") (properties "still-little"))
  (clause (text "The specification delegates this to the EEI;") (limits "that the specification delegates this to the EEI is the source's statement, and the pinned binary offers no other choice to compare"))
  (clause (text "endianness in RISC-V is byte-address invariant.") (properties "invariant-byte") (properties "invariant-word")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-FENCE")
  (clause (text "FENCE is decoded and must not trap.") (properties "fence-rw-rw"))
  (clause (text "With one hart, no external devices and an in-order model, it has no observable effect.") (properties "fence-iorw") (limits "no other hart or device exists here to observe an ordering, so a fence's effect is its absence from what one hart sees"))
  (clause (text "FENCE.TSO (fm=1000, pred=RW, succ=RW) is accepted and treated as FENCE RW,RW, which the specification states is correct.") (properties "fence-tso") (properties "fence-tso-reserved"))
  (clause (text "The remaining fm, pred and succ configurations are reserved, and the architecture SPECIFIES their behavior: base implementations shall treat all such reserved configurations as FENCE instructions (with fm = 0000) — they decode and execute as an ordinary FENCE, which under this profile has no observable effect.") (properties "fence-empty") (properties "fence-tso-reserved") (properties "fence-fm-reserved") (properties "fence-fm-top"))
  (clause (text "They do NOT fall under D-RESERVED-DECODE, and the rs1 and rd fields are ignored for forward compatibility, as the same section directs.") (properties "fence-rs1-rd-ignored") (properties "rd-kept") (properties "rs1-kept")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-D-WALK-IMPLICIT")
  (clause (text "When address translation is active (satp.MODE=Sv39), the hart's implicit memory accesses are the instruction fetch AND the translation algorithm's page-table reads: up to LEVELS (3) implicit 8-byte reads per access, each crossing the environment boundary as the walk-access kind, never silently as a data load.") (properties "walk-three") (properties "walk-two") (limits "the order and number of reads are not compared, since TLB replacement is not architectural; which PTEs are read, their values, their width and the absence of writes are the retained walk record's"))
  (clause (text "Under Svade the permitted page-table side effects are NONE: no implicit writes, ever.") (properties "leaf-unchanged") (properties "pointer-unchanged") (properties "root-unchanged") (properties "store-needs-d"))
  (clause (text "This AMENDS the implicit-access vocabulary for the translated composition: the base corpus's REQ-D-FETCH-IMPLICIT stays true of rv64i-lab-v0 (no translation exists there), and rv64gc's catalogue never carried it — measured: the mirror's closure is 13 records and it is not among them.") (limits "what the base corpus's requirement says of rv64i-lab-v0, and the mirror's closure, are catalogue facts, not behaviour a run can witness")))

(trace (requirement_id "REQ-GC-PARTIAL-PROGRESS")
  (clause (text "Every instruction completes or faults as a unit - the laboratory's declared preciseness (the pinned introduction leaves preciseness to the execution environment and recommends it):") (properties "hartid-before") (properties "csr-write-cause") (properties "load-cause") (properties "fload-cause") (properties "store-cause") (properties "amo-cause") (properties "sc-cause"))
  (clause (text "a delivered synchronous exception leaves the architectural state exactly as it was before the faulting instruction except for the trap report itself (xepc, xcause, xtval, the status stack, the mode, pc) -") (properties "load-tval"))
  (clause (text "no x- or f-register, CSR, fflags, FS, reservation or memory write of the faulting instruction is committed.") (properties "csr-rd-kept") (properties "load-rd-kept") (properties "f-before") (properties "f-kept") (properties "fflags-kept") (properties "fs-kept") (properties "store-memory-kept") (properties "amo-rd-kept") (properties "amo-memory-kept") (properties "lr-takes") (properties "sc-rd-kept") (properties "reservation-kept"))
  (clause (text "The reads that reached the environment before the fault are NOT rolled back and are declared, not hidden: a translation's earlier walk reads and its TLB fill, a page-straddling fetch's first parcel, and an atomic memory operation's completed load when its store is refused - each a read that changes no architectural state.") (limits "the reads themselves are not observed in this vocabulary: a walk's are REQ-D-WALK-IMPLICIT's record, and a straddling fetch's first parcel and an AMO's completed load are the corpus's"))
  (clause (text "No suboperation is restartable and no partial commit is possible.") (limits "that no suboperation is restartable is a claim over the whole engine, not one program"))
  (clause (text "Positive fixtures: inj-carrier, inj-atomics, inj-fp, inj-walk-l2, inj-walk-l1, inj-walk-l0 (faults injected at a chosen suboperation through the typed carrier), mm-csr-ro-write, prio-sv39.") (limits "the fixtures the statement names are the corpus's: a fault injected at a chosen suboperation is past the reference"))
  (clause (text "Negative evidence: the parent engine fails mm-csr-ro-write (it committed rd and then trapped), and the corpus fails when the carrier is ignored or a refused walk read becomes a page fault.") (limits "the negative evidence the statement names is the corpus's own")))
